# {{ s.name }} — Shader/Material Controller

**Variant:** {{ variant }}

{{ s.description }}

Drives `{{ s.property_name }}` via a **MaterialPropertyBlock** — the shared
Material asset is never touched, so no per-instance material leaks.

## Setup

{% if variant == "color_cycle" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject with a **Renderer** (MeshRenderer, SpriteRenderer, etc.).
2. Cycles through {{ s.stops | length }} color stop(s) on `{{ s.property_name }}`, looping: **{{ s.loop }}**.
3. Call `Play()` / `Stop()` to control the cycle at runtime.
{% for stop in s.stops %}
   - Stop {{ loop.index }}: RGBA({{ stop.r }}, {{ stop.g }}, {{ stop.b }}, {{ stop.a }}), hold {{ stop.hold }}s
{% endfor %}
{% elif variant == "dissolve" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject whose material exposes a dissolve-style float property (`{{ s.property_name }}`).
2. Sweeps 0 → 1 over {{ s.duration }}s. Auto-starts on `Start()`: **{{ s.auto_start }}**.
3. Call `Dissolve()` to sweep out, `Appear()` to sweep in.
{% elif variant == "hit_flash" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject with a **Renderer**.
2. Call `Flash()` (e.g. from a damage handler) to tint `{{ s.property_name }}` to RGB({{ s.flash_color_r }}, {{ s.flash_color_g }}, {{ s.flash_color_b }}) for {{ s.flash_duration }}s, then restore the original color.
{% elif variant == "uv_scroll" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject with a **Renderer** whose material has a texture property (`{{ s.property_name }}`).
2. Continuously scrolls the UV offset at ({{ s.speed_x }}, {{ s.speed_y }}) units/sec.
3. Call `SetSpeed(x, y)` to change scroll speed at runtime.
{% elif variant == "outline_pulse" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject with a **Renderer** whose material exposes an outline/rim float property (`{{ s.property_name }}`).
2. Pulses sinusoidally between {{ s.min_value }} and {{ s.max_value }} at speed {{ s.pulse_speed }}.
3. Call `SetRange(min, max)` to change the pulse bounds at runtime.
{% endif %}
